counterexample:
Loop counters, accumulators, and ongoing state updates whose semantic role remains constant are legitimate mutable bindings:
```rust
let mut total_revenue = 0;
for item in transactions {
    total_revenue += item.amount;
}
```

fix:
Introduce separately named immutable values for the distinct concepts and update each consumer to use the intended one. Leave input parameters intact when later code may need the original values; retain mutation only for true accumulators or evolving values with one stable meaning.
```rust
fn calculate_physics(mass: f64, primary_force: f64, secondary_force: f64) {
    let primary_acc = primary_force / mass;
    println!("Primary acceleration: {}", primary_acc);

    let combined_acc = (primary_force + secondary_force) / mass;
    println!("Secondary acceleration: {}", combined_acc);
}

fn calculate_total(input_value: f64) -> f64 {
    let price_with_tax = input_value * 1.08;
    price_with_tax
}
